# InterMUN Intentional UI Rule

Use the SEAMUN Chat visual language as the source of truth for **all** UI (landing, app chrome, documents, prototypes). Designs should feel premium, calm, and human — not templated.

## Color & Tone
- Background base: pastel blue `#DFF2FC` with soft wash to `#EDF8FF` / `#F8FBFF`
- Ink: `#183148` · soft ink `#35516B` · muted `#6A7D91`
- Navy brand panels / primary CTAs: `#17324A` (hover `#244964`)
- Accent (selected / links): `#119ED3`
- Borders: `#C9DDE9` · raised surface `#FFFDF8`
- Soft blue-tinted shadows only — never harsh black glows

## Typography
- Display / headings: **Instrument Serif**
- Body / UI: **Inter Tight**
- Mix serif display with tight sans body; 2–3 natural heading scales
- Avoid Poppins + Inter + Manrope stacks

## Layout & Composition
- Auth / gates: split navy brand panel + white form (desktop)
- Prefer asymmetry / staggered sections; intentional whitespace
- Never clone identical section structures back-to-back

## Buttons & Microcopy
- Primary = navy filled; secondary = soft bordered / glass
- Descriptive CTAs; conversational copy
- Subtle hover lift — no glowing edges

## Cards & Components
- Softer radii (~12–24px); soft pastel borders
- Keep existing component naming/IA intact
- Enhance only via color, texture, motion — do not change labels or structural naming

## Motion
- 300–500ms with staggered direction/delay
- Brand panel slides from left; form from right on auth/gates
